course: dictionary
lesson: 7660
title: Pronounce and its meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Pronounce means to say a word's sounds in a particular way. When you learn a new word, you also learn how to pronounce it, so people can understand you. «How do you pronounce Worcestershire?» asks about the sounds, not the meaning.
explain: Pronounce has other meanings too. It can mean to announce something officially, as in «The doctor pronounced him fit». It can also mean to give a judgement, as in «The judge pronounced the sentence». Look at the words around it to see which meaning is used.
explain: Context clues help. If the words around pronounce are about sounds, letters or saying a word, it means say the sounds. If they are about a doctor, a judge or a ceremony, it means declare officially. Swap in your meaning and check that the sentence still makes sense.
explain: «An accent is the way people pronounce words; a dialect is a local way of speaking with its own words and grammar.» Two children from different places may pronounce the same word differently, and both are speaking English.
fact: Pronounce means to say a word's sounds in a particular way.
fact: «I now pronounce you husband and wife» is a formal use: it means announce officially.
fact: Silent letters are written but not said: the k in «knee» is silent.
fact: An accent is the way people pronounce words.
fact: A dialect is a local way of speaking, with its own words and sometimes its own grammar.
fact: Britain and Ireland have many dialects, sometimes changing every few miles.
exercise: In «How do you pronounce Worcestershire?», what is being asked about? | *The sounds of the word | How many times the word is used | Who first wrote the word down | The meaning of a sauce
exercise: «The doctor pronounced him fit.» What does pronounced mean here? | Shouted loudly | *Officially declared | Wrote it in a notebook | Said the sounds of a word
exercise: In «knee», which letter is silent? | e | All of them are said | n | *k
test: «The judge pronounced the sentence.» What does pronounced mean here? | *Gave the official judgement | Said the sounds of the word | Lost the paper it was written on | Whispered it quietly
test: What is a dialect? | A type of cake | *A local way of speaking, with its own words and sometimes grammar | The sound a single letter makes | A way of spelling a word
exam: Which meaning fits pronounce in the sentence «Say the word slowly so I can pronounce it»? | Give a judgement | *Say the sounds | Declare officially | Write it down
